# Copy to `.env.local` (which git ignores) to run the tests that need real Aurora data.
# `npm test` reads `.env.local` when it exists. Nothing here is required: a test whose data is not
# configured is skipped, and CI sets these itself. Once a variable is set, a path that does not exist
# fails the run instead of skipping it, because a skipped test is a green one.
#
# The AuroraLegacy.index to read. In an Aurora install it is under `custom/`. Never commit the real
# value: a path names a person's machine and version-control history is permanent.
INCUDO_AURORA_INDEX="/path/to/Aurora/custom/AuroraLegacy.index"

# The folder of your own `.dnd5e` saves. Optional: for an Aurora install it defaults to the folder that
# holds `custom/`. Saves are personal data and can never be committed, so tests that read them
# only run where you put them.
# INCUDO_AURORA_SAVES="/path/to/your/saves"

# Print every difference the Aurora oracle finds, for chasing an `element-extra`.
# INCUDO_ORACLE_DETAIL=1
